    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nFrankly I never use saw<surrounding>, saaw<surrounding>. Mostly just saiw<surroundings>.  So having 5 keystroke to surround a word basically is too much overhead for me. Also saw<...>  has nice ring to it, \"surround around word (with) <...>.\n\nSo it would be great to have ability to overload text object w , W with \"iw\", and \"iW\" etc.",
