    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe \"add\" operator in 'mini.surround' acts as any other operator. As in 1) it expects textobject/motion defined via following keystrokes and 2) it has no control over how they are defined.\n\nThe only (reasonably) way to achieve this is to create custom Operator-pending mode mappings. Like `vim.keymap.set('o', 'w', 'iw')`, etc. But not that this will have effect outside of 'mini.surround'.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
